l":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.6.3.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.3.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.7.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Apple M1 - Apple M1 (8 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen vsync is turned on, the macOS VoiceOver screenreader becomes extremely slow (taking about a second to respond to each keypress).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUsing the minimal reproduction project below, make a Mac build and try using VoiceOver to navigate between the buttons.\n\nIf you go back into the Godot Project > Project settings, search for vsync, and disable V-Sync Mode. Make another Mac build and notice that the problem goes away.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThis tiny project demonstrates the problem:\n\nhttps://github.com/PeterDrake/screenreader","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120211/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120211/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}